BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 692.00 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 669.77 Tm (Supplier concentration is the trap that bit the biggest numbers. Brook Hiddink's first supplier generated over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 654.55 Tm ($2M, roughly half of all sales, then shut its dealer program in June 2023; Brook moved the store to a new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.32 Tm (domain, ran it about 8 months, and an own-brand project is now paused after 8 months of sampling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.10 Tm ([8V2vAoy6GNA @ 00:27:19]. Kenny hit the mirror-image risk: two products from two brands drove 85-90%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.87 Tm (of revenue, and when a recall and manufacturing defect hit a roughly $2,000 product across the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 593.65 Tm (supplier, Kenny had to phone customers and make promises to hold the sales [91zki-xXArY @ 00:24:02].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.42 Tm (Joe Verschoor reports the gate itself tightening, with suppliers now harder to land because bad actors took) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.20 Tm (lines of credit and never paid invoices [uxvzRhKmdXU @ 00:09:09]. Asonjf adds two structural killers:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.97 Tm (businesses fail when suppliers cut product quality to fatten their own margin, and big-box sellers like Best) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 532.75 Tm (Buy, Home Depot, Lowe's and Walmart buy in bulk, are not bound by the same dealer agreement, and will) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 517.52 Tm (undercut you and outbid you on ads [r79NEO4JF2M @ 00:05:34]. Brook's answer is to name stores broadly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.30 Tm (so every added supplier becomes a separate income stream, such as $20k from one brand plus $20-30k a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.07 Tm (month from another.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.85 Tm (Cash and post-sale exposure punish operators who only model the front end. Ecommerce Paradise warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 456.62 Tm (chargebacks take 30 to 60 days to resolve, banks sometimes side with the customer, and those high-ticket) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.40 Tm (disputes 'can really eat away at your margins and your cash flow,' on top of restocking fees, return shipping,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.17 Tm (non-returnable custom or medical items, and warranties that cover parts but not labor [EaAeDMJIPLQ @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.95 Tm (00:02:06]. Ecommerce Paradise also tells operators to absorb costs when needed to protect reviews.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 395.72 Tm (Marcus Lam describes $200K a month in low-ticket revenue lost to chargebacks, and his student Johnny) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 380.50 Tm (then found many tested high-ticket brands unprofitable once shipping was priced in, forcing a niche-down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.27 Tm (onto a new domain and a supplier purge [7B1m62WaDkw @ 00:04:43]. Joe Verschoor refuses blanket free) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.05 Tm (shipping because 'you can't offer free shipping if you're going to end up losing money because of it,') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.82 Tm (especially on LTL freight shipments [5jY7d_1m1t0 @ 00:05:07]. MAP cuts both ways: WatchMeDropship) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.60 Tm (says breaking it usually gets the wholesale account pulled, while Ali never made substantial revenue in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.37 Tm (niches without strict MAP, expects about 90% compliance at best, and warns 'you're probably going to lose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.15 Tm (a lot of money on some deals' [pbk_t9e4Xpo @ 00:23:17].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.92 Tm (Timeline and effort are where expectations break. Brook Hiddink tells students to assume zero sales in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 258.70 Tm (month one on roughly $500 of ads, says most quit at about two weeks in the uninformed-pessimism stage,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.47 Tm (and calls it a big mistake to think switching on ads makes sales pour in; Brook also watched 5 to 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.25 Tm (copycats a day walk the store's abandoned-checkout sequence [8V2vAoy6GNA @ 00:31:03]. Ali's own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.02 Tm (record is 8 to 10 stores with the first succeeding and 5 to 6 failing afterward, and he tells beginners to expect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.80 Tm (1 to 2 months to a first sale, even though his recent stores now hit one in about two weeks [pbk_t9e4Xpo @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 182.57 Tm (00:08:08]. Kenny underestimated the ad bill, guessing $2-3k when the dashboard showed $4,376.72, still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.35 Tm (handles customer service personally, and prices a full-time VA at $400-500 a month, so the model is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 152.12 Tm (passive [91zki-xXArY @ 00:28:59]. Joe Verschoor keeps the profit math honest: $300k months at about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 136.90 Tm (20% gross yield $40-60k profit and are not the norm, some stores only break even, and a realistic net lands) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 121.67 Tm (at 15 to 20% of revenue, with $10k net months arriving around month six to eight, sometimes four to six) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.45 Tm ([5jY7d_1m1t0 @ 00:07:16].) Tj ET
